    "observedCues": {
      "firstCourse": "A P Switch's Journey. The visible P Switch travels along a separate upper route while Mario runs below. At 42.009s Mario is next to the switch on the lower platform with the block column still present. At 42.509s the switch is gone and coins occupy the column. Around 43.510s Mario passes that opening.",
      "secondCourse": "Switch It Up! The block column becomes coins at about 101.5s while the visible P Switch is still ahead. Mario advances across the top, the area switches back to blocks by 104.504s, and Mario follows the layered route past spikes. A later sampled change returns part of the lower route to coins. Show visible alternating states and navigation without claiming the initial change was triggered by Mario's direct contact.",
      "limits": "The courses show uses of the same switch-related rule at different levels of surrounding complexity. They do not establish a publisher's actual design sequence, a simple first tutorial, the original team's intentions or measured difficulty. Separate the released clips from our controlled hazard demonstration."
